<article class="env-lemma" id="0B3U">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B3U">Lemma <span data-tag="0B3U">31.31.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a quasi-coherent graded $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebra. Let $p : X = \underline{\text{Proj}}_ S(\mathcal{A}) \to S$ be the relative Proj of $\mathcal{A}$. If $\mathcal{A}$ is generated by $\mathcal{A}_1$ over $\mathcal{A}_0$ and $\mathcal{A}_1$ is a finite type $\mathcal{O}_ S$-module, then $p$ is projective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, the morphism associated to the graded $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebra map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Sym}_{\mathcal{O}_ X}^*(\mathcal{A}_1) \longrightarrow \mathcal{A}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is a closed immersion $X \to \mathbf{P}(\mathcal{A}_1)$, see Constructions, Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZK" data-tag="07ZK">27.18.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>